 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Definitely. Look for laptops with a hinge that lets you swap out the pad yourself, and get one with a touch pad you can turn off. Yes, a laptop you can use with one hand is much better than one that pulls your arm out. Some come with a clicky button instead of a pad, which some people find better. Try one at shop if you can. Some keyboards have a little button you press to switch between modes. Look at the keyboard layout, some are designed for right handed people. And check the battery life, it's usually lower on lefties.",
